      "message": "feat(motion): air-side stock ring planner for the adaptive pocket\n\nRound A of #1950. plan_from_air cuts the stock ring of a level from\nthe air side: fronts are inward offsets of the stock outline by one\nstep width; closed fronts join as a ramped spiral, fronts broken by\nthe part wall are cut as open runs with measured lead-ins (a run is\ncut short where no lead-in holds the load), then two offset wall laps\nand the outline lap. Raster::open_air opens the air band. The raster\nwalks move to raster/walk.rs (400-line rule, no logic change).\n\nNot wired into hsm_passes yet (round B). Pinned by the four air_rings\ntests on the user's D plate: worst load 0.1538 = the limit, rest 0,\n10537 moves.\n\nRefs #1950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
