      "message": "feat(motion): route the stock outline to the air-side ring planner\n\nRound B of issue #1950 (plumbing only).\n\n- open_sides takes a stock band; stock_band(r, adaptive) gives 2r +\n  OPEN_SLACK for Adaptive and the old r - OPEN_SLACK for every other\n  strategy (computed exactly as before).\n- New entry pocket3d_open_prev; the stock argument goes through\n  ladder, plan_level (None on the wrap), adaptive_passes and\n  hsm_passes.\n- hsm_passes plans a piece that reaches past the stock from the air\n  (plan_from_air), the material clipped to the stock; a plan over the\n  load bound is refused by name (degree compare, 1e-9 slack, as\n  lift::keeps) and the level goes to the Offset rings, said.\n- The probe becomes pins: the stock ring level reaches the air\n  planner, no stock keeps the growth spiral, an overloaded air plan\n  is refused by name.\n\nNo app arm calls the new entry yet: posted G-code does not change.\n\nRefs #1950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
